job_description:
Head of Spatial Modelling & Research
Department: Cities & Regions
Employment Type: Full Time
Location: London, UK

Description
Oxford Economics, a leading economic forecasting and consulting firm, is looking to hire a technically skilled economist to join our team and lead the technical implementation and continued development of our economic forecasting models and geospatial analytics capabilities. This is a leadership role, with a small technical research team reporting directly to the successful candidate. The team will play a fundamental part in supporting the wider cities team, and is expected to grow over time. The role will focus on leading and line-managing that team in developing scalable analytical pipelines for quantitative modelling and steering our technical research into the use of emerging data science and spatial analytics techniques within our city and regional economic monitoring and forecasting services.

The cities team consists of around 40 economists and data scientists who help clients understand the structure and outlook of thousands of locations across all parts of the world, as well as quantifying key risks under different economic scenarios and climate pathways. The team supports its client base through a range of subscription services and consultancy projects. The client base is global, and includes firms in the real estate sector, financial services, B2C companies, think tanks, and government/public sector organisations.

The successful candidate will work with a multidisciplinary team to conduct in-depth research focused on the intersection of economics and geospatial data. They will be responsible for developing, implementing, and maintaining complex economic forecasting models and associated data pipelines, combining economic theory, econometrics, and geospatial analytics. The ideal candidate will have strong technical expertise in data analysis and economic modelling, and the ability to use AI-assisted coding tools to accelerate model development, testing, and maintenance. In the role, they will collaborate with other teams at Oxford Economics, utilising different expertise to provide powerful solutions. The role involves working with diverse clients worldwide and therefore strong written and verbal communication skills are essential. The role also offers opportunities for international travel, including representing Oxford Economics as a speaker at relevant conferences and industry events.

The role will suit candidates with a strong academic background in economics, geography, data science, or a related discipline, and those with at least 10 years’ experience undertaking relevant work.

This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced individual to shape the direction of a growing research team. We offer a rewarding work environment with room for growth, a highly competitive salary package (including bonus plan), and an excellent benefits package.

Key Responsibilities

• Lead the technical implementation and development of economic forecasting models, including city, regional, and hyperlocal applications;

• Ensure that Oxford Economics’ city forecasting models and analytical pipelines are technically robust, scalable, and aligned with the latest methodological developments;

• Present research findings to internal teams, clients, and stakeholders with clear, actionable recommendations, and raise the profile of our spatial research by securing and delivering speaking opportunities at relevant events, including internationally;

• Stay updated on the latest trends and methodologies in economics, data science, and geospatial technologies;

• Line-manage and lead a small team of economists and data scientists, setting priorities, planning and structuring technical development projects, and coordinating the team’s contributions;

• Take responsibility for the professional development of direct reports, sharing knowledge and expertise, mentoring junior colleagues, and bringing new ideas and techniques to the team;

• Design, code, implement, and maintain quantitative models to assess economic performance, spatial disparities, and the impact of geographic factors on economic activities;

• Develop and maintain complex modelling pipelines using Python and AI-assisted coding tools and agents, with a focus on efficient, reproducible, and scalable analytical workflows;

• Work with large-scale geospatial, economic, demographic, and company-level datasets, integrating them with economic indicators to generate actionable insights.

Skills, Knowledge & Expertise
The successful candidate will be expected to have at least 10 years of prior experience in quantitative economic modelling or data science, with a strong track record of developing and implementing complex analytical models.

The successful candidate will be rigorous, adaptable, and creative in seeking solutions to difficult economic questions and should also have the following essential attributes:

• Strong academic education in economics, geography, data science, or a related discipline;

• Advanced programming skills, particularly in Python, alongside proficiency in geospatial analysis tools and spatial data libraries;

• Experience developing and implementing quantitative economic or demographic forecasting models;

• Experience with econometric, statistical forecasting, and other quantitative methods;

• In-depth knowledge of economic concepts, issues, and analytical techniques relevant to sub-national analysis;

• Ability to manage technical development tasks independently, coordinate with colleagues, and deliver robust analytical solutions to agreed timelines;

• Strong written and verbal communication skills, including experience in explaining technical concepts and quantitative results to non-specialists;

• Proven experience managing and developing a team, including line management, sharing technical expertise, reviewing code, and supporting the development of junior colleagues;

• Experience using AI-assisted coding tools and agents to support software development, debugging, testing, and documentation, with an understanding of the importance of independent validation and quality assurance;

• Ability to problem-solve and produce innovative analysis across a range of different projects and challenges, including spatial, conceptual, strategic, and economic issues;

• Entrepreneurial and proactive in identifying emerging business opportunities, and developing ways for the team to pursue them;

• Ability to work independently and in cross-functional teams.

• The following would also be desirable:

• Experience developing forecasting models for city, regional, or small-area applications;

• Experience with spatial econometrics and other spatial modelling techniques;

• Experience leveraging machine learning techniques for both classification and regression outputs.

Job Benefits
Here are some of the benefits we offer in the UK to ensure you feel valued, supported, and thrive at work:

- Private Healthcare 
- Employee Assistance Program
- Enhanced Maternity and Paternity Leave 
- Workplace Nursery Scheme
- Cycle to Work Scheme

Oxford Economics is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, colour, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by the law.

A vacancy has arisen to join Billington Structures Ltd (Wombwell) as a Senior Design Engineer

Hours of work: 37.5 per week

## The Company

Billington Structures is one of the UK’s leading structural steelwork specialists designing, manufacturing and constructing a wide portfolio of projects to a variety of clients, established for over 75 years with a professional and dynamic team. 

Our experienced workforce can tackle projects from simple building frames to the most complex structures. With plants in Barnsley South Yorkshire, we have the capability to process 50,000 tonnes of steel per annum, and are able to service clients at locations throughout the UK and Europe. 

## Role Purpose

We are looking to recruit a Senior Design Engineer responsible for the following...

- • To design, analyse, and deliver safe, efficient, and compliant structural engineering solutions that support project objectives, meet client requirements, and adhere to relevant industry standards and regulations. The Structural Engineer is responsible for ensuring the structural integrity, buildability, and cost-effectiveness of projects while collaborating with multidisciplinary teams to achieve high-quality outcomes within agreed timelines and budgets.

## Role Responsibilities

- • Work closely with clients, colleagues and other professionals, using construction plans, drawings and specifications;
- • Develop design ideas using current industry software;
- • Apply loadings to and calculate stresses and load paths through different parts of a structure;
- • Ensure that projects meet legal guidelines, environmental directives, and health and safety requirements;
- • Prepare bids for tenders;
- • Maintain quality service by following company standards;
- • Maintain professional and technical knowledge by attending educational workshops; reviewing professional publications; establishing personal networks; participating in professional societies;
- • Contribute to team effort by accomplishing related results as needed;
- • Provide progress reports to clients and senior managers;

## Skills, Experience and Qualifications

- • Robust knowledge of structural mechanics and engineering principles,
- • Excellent design calculation capabilities and experience of using sector-related software packages such as Tekla Structural Designer (Fastrak Building Designer), Fastrak Portal Frame, Masterframe / STAAD PRO, Masterseries Connections etc..
- • Extensive experience in working within a structural design role, preferably also with experience in connection design.

## Salary and Benefits

Salary will be dependent on experience, and we offer a competitive benefits package including company pension, sick pay scheme, health plan, cycle to work scheme, share save scheme and the option to purchase additional holidays.

About the Company:

At Playlist, life's richest moments happen when people step away from screens to move, connect, explore, and play. We're building the definitive platform for intentional living, connecting people with inspiring experiences in fitness, wellness, and beyond. With popular brands like Mindbody and ClassPass, Playlist empowers businesses and individuals, making it effortless for aspirations to become actions. Join us in reshaping technology's role to foster meaningful, real-world connections.

The Role You’ll Play:&nbsp;

As a Data Scientist, you will play a critical role in driving insights and building data products that support large-scale, cross-departmental initiatives. You’ll combine advanced statistical inference, strong engineering skills, and business intuition to create models and tools that improve marketplace efficiency, retention, and growth. This role is not about building models in isolation—it’s about leveraging data science to influence strategy, fuel automation, and deliver measurable business impact.&nbsp;

• Partner with Product, Marketing, Operations, and Finance teams to design and execute analytical solutions that optimize marketplace dynamics, improve unit economics, and uncover opportunities for growth.&nbsp;

• Apply statistical inference and causal modeling to evaluate experiments, quantify business impact, and guide decision-making under uncertainty.&nbsp;

• Design, prototype, and deploy scalable data products such as anomaly detection systems, prioritization algorithms, and similarity/recommendation models.&nbsp;

• Translate complex models and findings into actionable insights and clear recommendations for business stakeholders, including executives.&nbsp;

• Build frameworks for experimentation, measurement, and monitoring that drive iteration and continuous improvement of strategic initiatives.&nbsp;

• Balance hands-on technical work (modeling, coding, automation) with strategic thinking, ensuring data science investments align with business objectives.&nbsp;

• Act as a technical thought partner and mentor for analysts and junior data scientists, raising the bar on scientific rigor and reproducibility.&nbsp;

Experience You Bring:&nbsp;

• 3–5 years of experience in data science, applied statistics, or a related quantitative discipline, ideally within marketplace or platform businesses.&nbsp;

• Strong expertise in statistical inference, causal modeling, and experiment design, with the ability to draw robust conclusions from noisy or incomplete data.&nbsp;

• &nbsp;Proficiency in Python (pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, statsmodels, PySpark, etc.) and SQL, with experience building and deploying production-grade models.&nbsp;

• Proven track record of designing and delivering data products such as anomaly detectors, ranking/prioritization models, similarity or recommendation systems.&nbsp;

• Familiarity architecting automated pipelines and data flows that support machine learning and analytics at scale.&nbsp;

• Ability to balance technical depth with business acumen—knowing when a simple solution beats a complex one, and when complexity is necessary to win.&nbsp;

• Strong communication and storytelling skills, with the ability to influence non-technical stakeholders and executives.&nbsp;

• Comfort with ambiguity and a fast-paced environment; you thrive on experimentation, iteration, and turning insights into action.&nbsp;

• Familiarity with data visualization and dashboarding tools (e.g., Tableau, Looker, Power BI) to communicate insights effectively.&nbsp;

• Internally competitive and externally collaborative&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Have we piqued your curiosity?

Sound like the role for you? We’d love to hear from you! Even if you’re not 100% sure about potential fit, we still encourage you to apply. We’re looking for the right person, not the perfect series of checkboxes.

The Company is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We highly value diversity at our company and encourage people of all different backgrounds, experiences, abilities and perspectives to apply. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or other protected characteristics.

By entering your email and phone number and submitting your application, you consent to receive emails, calls and SMS about your application and other roles at The Company, including by auto-dialer. Message and data rates may apply. Opt-out or text STOP to cancel at any time. If you are a California resident or reside outside the United States then by submitting your application you confirm that you have read, understood, agree and - where applicable - grant your prior, free, informed and express consent for the processing of your personal information, including sensitive personal information, as described in our California Applicant Privacy Notice&nbsp;or&nbsp;International Applicant Privacy Notice (as applicable).

Note: This description outlines key responsibilities but isn’t intended&nbsp;to cover every task or duty. Additional responsibilities may be&nbsp;assigned as needed to support the team and business goals.

Policy Expert – Customer Experience Manager&nbsp;

🚀Are you ready to transform the insurance industry?&nbsp;

Policy Expert is a forward-thinking business that loves to get things done. Leveraging proprietary technology and smart data, we offer reliable products and a wow customer experience.&nbsp;

Having achieved rapid growth since being founded in 2011, we’ve won over 1.5 million customers in Home, Motor and Pet insurance and have been ranked the UK’s No.1-rated home insurer by Review Centre since 2013. 🏆&nbsp;

Hear from our team about what it's like working at Policy Expert ✨

Reporting to the Customer Experience Lead, the Customer Experience Manager is responsible for managing and improving customer journeys across the customer lifecycle, ensuring customers receive clear, effective and compliant experiences at every interaction. &nbsp;

Working across Retail, Technology, Service &amp; Operations and other business functions, the role combines customer insight, journey management and communication skills to identify improvement opportunities and help deliver better customer outcomes. &nbsp;

The role plays a key part in turning customer insight into practical improvements, using customer feedback, operational insight and performance data to shape journey enhancements, communications and experience improvements. This includes customer journey communications, product webpages, communication governance, consumer understanding testing and maintaining a strong focus on vulnerable customer needs and regulatory expectations. &nbsp;

Success in the role comes from balancing customer outcomes, operational effectiveness and commercial opportunities, while working closely with the CX Lead and multiple stakeholders to deliver measurable improvements to the customer experience.&nbsp;

Your day to day:&nbsp;

• Mapping, documenting and managing customer journeys across key customer interactions and touchpoints. &nbsp;

• Identifying and delivering customer experience improvements using feedback from Customer Outcomes, Service &amp; Operations and other insight sources. This will include analysing customer data and performance information to generate insights and drive action plans. &nbsp;

• Developing lifecycle communication briefs and identifying opportunities to improve customer engagement, retention and commercial performance. &nbsp;

• Managing customer journey communications (e.g. emails, webpages, scripts), including design, copywriting, editing and optimisation across purchase, service, and claims journeys. &nbsp;

• Managing customer-facing product webpages, ensuring content remains accurate, effective and aligned to customer needs. &nbsp;

• Conducting consumer understanding reviews and testing activity, using findings to improve customer comprehension and outcomes. &nbsp;

• Updating communication governance through communication logs, reviews and compliance oversight. &nbsp;

• Championing fair treatment and positive outcomes for vulnerable customers across journeys and communications.&nbsp;

Who are you:&nbsp;

• Someone who naturally puts the customer at the centre of decision-making, whilst balancing commercial objectives, operational realities and regulatory requirements. &nbsp;

• Has proven experience improving customer journeys, communications or customer experience programmes, and be comfortable working across multiple teams to turn insight into action. Equally happy analysing data as reviewing customer communications, you'll enjoy identifying opportunities, solving problems and driving continuous improvement. &nbsp;

• Confident challenging existing ways of working and collaborating closely with stakeholders towards a shared customer goal. Strong organisational skills and attention to detail are important, as you'll often be managing multiple priorities, projects and communications at the same time. &nbsp;

It will be a bonus if you have: &nbsp;

• Experience working in B2C financial services or another regulated service-based environment. &nbsp;

• A good understanding of Consumer Duty principles and the importance of delivering good customer outcomes.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• A good understanding of vulnerable customer considerations and how these should be reflected in journeys and communications.&nbsp; &nbsp;

Benefits:&nbsp;

📍 This role will be based in our London office in a 50/50 Hybrid mode.&nbsp;

💸 We match your pension contributions up to 7%&nbsp;

🏥 Private medical &amp; Dental cover&nbsp;

📚 Learning budget of £1,000 a year + Study leave (with encouragement to use it)&nbsp;

😁 Enhanced maternity &amp; paternity&nbsp;&nbsp;

🚉 Travel season ticket loan&nbsp;

🎟️ Access to a wide selection of London O2 events and use of a Private Lounge&nbsp;

🌈 Employee Wellbeing Programme&nbsp;

🚪 Prayer room in Office&nbsp;

What We Stand for and Next Steps “We pride ourselves on being an equal opportunity employer. We treat all applications equally and recruit based solely on an individual’s skills, knowledge, and experience. The quality and growing diversity of our team is a testament to this commitment” &nbsp;

At Policy Expert, we are committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive environment for all candidates. If you require any reasonable adjustments during the interview process to accommodate your needs, please do not hesitate to let us know. We are dedicated to ensuring every candidate has an equal opportunity to succeed and will work with you to provide the necessary support.&nbsp;

We aim to be in touch within 14 working days of your application – you will be notified if successful or unsuccessful. Please be encouraged to apply even if you do not meet all the requirements.&nbsp;

Policy Expert – Digital Optimisation Manager&nbsp;

🚀Are you ready to transform the insurance industry?&nbsp;

Policy Expert is a forward-thinking business that loves to get things done. Leveraging proprietary technology and smart data, we offer reliable products and a wow customer experience.&nbsp;

Having achieved rapid growth since being founded in 2011, we’ve won over 1.5 million customers in Home, Motor and Pet insurance and have been ranked the UK’s No.1-rated home insurer by Review Centre since 2013. 🏆&nbsp;

Hear from our team about what it's like working at Policy Expert ✨

Your day to day:&nbsp;

• Own our optimisation programme across all our brands, products and tiers. You’ll set the roadmap and prioritise the biggest opportunities to improve customer and commercial outcomes. &nbsp;

• Keep value versus volume at the heart of every decision. You’ll judge ideas and test results on what they’re worth to us, not just how many more sales they bring. &nbsp;

• &nbsp;Keep improving customer journeys, using performance data and customer insight to find and remove friction. &nbsp;

• Turn opportunities into clear hypotheses and run experiments from start to finish in Optimizely. That covers test design, success measures, execution, analysis and recommendations. &nbsp;

• Balance quick wins with bigger ideas that could change performance, and turn successful tests into improvements we can roll out at scale. &nbsp;

• Use ContentSquare to understand how customers behave, from setting up mapping through to reporting. &nbsp;

• Use GA4 and BigQuery to measure results and spot trends, and help shape the tagging we need to track performance properly. &nbsp;

• Use tools like Claude to speed up analysis, generate ideas and make reporting quicker. &nbsp;

• Work closely with teams across the business to agree priorities, get tests live and share what we learn. &nbsp;

• Explain results and recommendations clearly to stakeholders at every level, and help build a strong test-and-learn culture. &nbsp;

• Be our go-to expert on optimisation and experimentation.&nbsp;

Who are you:&nbsp;

• You’re an experienced optimisation specialist, ready to take the next step into running the programme. &nbsp;

• Hands-on experience of Optimizely (essential). &nbsp;

• Experience of ContentSquare, from mapping set-up to reporting, is preferable. &nbsp;

• Experience of GA4 is preferable. Tagging experience would be an advantage. &nbsp;

• An excellent understanding of value versus volume, and how to balance them when prioritising work and judging tests. &nbsp;

• Financial services experience is preferable.&nbsp;

• A subject matter expert who can explain experimentation in plain terms to non-specialists. &nbsp;

• A self-starter who works autonomously. You’ll own your programme and keep it moving without needing to be directed. &nbsp;

• Comfortable working across multiple products, tiers and brands, and keeping priorities straight between them. &nbsp;

• Collaborative and confident working with lots of different teams.&nbsp;

Benefits:&nbsp;

📍 This role will be based in our London office in a 50/50 Hybrid mode.&nbsp;

💸 We match your pension contributions up to 7%&nbsp;

🏥 Private medical &amp; Dental cover&nbsp;

📚 Learning budget of £1,000 a year + Study leave (with encouragement to use it)&nbsp;

😁 Enhanced maternity &amp; paternity&nbsp;&nbsp;

🚉 Travel season ticket loan&nbsp;

🎟️ Access to a wide selection of London O2 events and use of a Private Lounge&nbsp;

🌈 Employee Wellbeing Programme&nbsp;

🚪 Prayer room in Office&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What We Stand for and Next Steps “We pride ourselves on being an equal opportunity employer. We treat all applications equally and recruit based solely on an individual’s skills, knowledge, and experience. The quality and growing diversity of our team is a testament to this commitment” &nbsp;

At Policy Expert, we are committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive environment for all candidates. If you require any reasonable adjustments during the interview process to accommodate your needs, please do not hesitate to let us know. We are dedicated to ensuring every candidate has an equal opportunity to succeed and will work with you to provide the necessary support.&nbsp;

We aim to be in touch within 14 working days of your application – you will be notified if successful or unsuccessful. Please be encouraged to apply even if you do not meet all the requirements. &nbsp;

Positiv careers

 At Positiv Cohort, we’re a team of delivery-focused professionals supporting high-stakes projects in secure, complex environments. From engineering and software to cyber and transformation, we work where precision, trust, and outcomes matter most.

 We’re building a culture shaped by accountability, agility, and pride in the work we do. Our people are hand-picked for their expertise and mindset – professionals who thrive in environments where quality, rigour, and responsiveness are essential.
We’re proud to say we’re a genuinely good place to work – not just because of the projects we deliver, but because of how we treat each other.

 We value authenticity, support individuality, and believe that people do their best work when they’re respected, trusted, and backed by a team that cares.
We offer meaningful projects, supportive leadership, and the chance to grow your career while making a real impact.

 Interested in joining the Cohort?

