 Current Vacancies
Currently Recruiting: 
AI Officer
About Re: Agency
• Re: Agency is a brand building agency with offices in London and New York

• Re: Agency doesn’t have a type of client – we have a type of founder or team that we want to work with.

• Each of the businesses we represent have been started by someone whose ideas and ethos we admire and who wish to work collaboratively with us

• We love start-ups and are especially proud of those we have incubated and worked with from their inception. Many of these are now globally recognised names and players across tech, hospitality, lifestyle, travel, luxury and finance

• Creative ideas are at the heart of everything we do, working with press, influencers, brand partners and beyond to create strategies that are tailor-made and thoughtfully executed for each individual client. At Re: Agency, no day is ever the same

• Communications is entering a new phase, we aim to innovate. We want future-thinkers

An Ideal Candidate
• Our most successful team members are those who are creative, outside of the box thinkers, who are experts in spinning plates, who have their finger on the pulse and who thrive in social interaction / making new friends and connections

• Will be dialled in on the most current, culturally important people, events, brands and more – focused to both the UK and US markets

• Possess exceptional industry contacts and relationships in London and New York City (and beyond)

• High level execution skills and meticulous attention to detail, both aesthetically and organisationally

• Adaptable to a fast-paced, multi-task environment

• Ability to ‘spin plates’

• Confidence to make suggestions, bring ideas to the wider team that focuses on client experience and work alone or as part of a team

• Enthusiasm and motivation to attend industry events

• Strong communication skills (both written and oral), research, and organization skills

• A positive, can-do attitude who can work under pressure and likes to solve problems

• A creative, innovative thinker with an open attitude and eagerness to learn new things

AI Officer - London

Re: Agency is looking for an AI Officer to lead how we adopt, build and govern AI across the agency. You will turn new technology into practical tools that make our work faster, better, more consistent and more innovative, while keeping client data, our IP and our people safe.
The role sits where innovation, technology and AI meet. You will own the agency’s AI strategy and roadmap, run a central digital service that supports every team, and give colleagues the guidance, training and confidence to use new tools well.
Just as important is the culture you build. We want a team that is curious, tech-fluent and always learning, with no silos between disciplines. You will be the bridge between emerging technology and the quality of our work.
• Build and own a single AI and digital roadmap for the agency, aligned with business goals.

• Lead the adoption of generative AI and machine learning to support creative exploration, automate repetitive tasks and improve data-driven decisions.

• Track emerging tools and trends, and test the promising ones through small, measurable pilots.

• Report regularly to leadership on progress, value delivered and risks.

• Work with team leads to find where automation and AI can deliver clear, measurable value.

• Select, integrate and configure software, and build internal tools and workflows that improve efficiency, quality and consistency.

• Run a central digital service that supports every team, with clear standards, templates and documentation.

• Manage AI vendors, licences and budgets.

• Give colleagues the guidance, training and resources to adopt new tools with confidence.

• Act as the first point of contact for AI questions across the agency and its clients

• Own and enforce the agency’s AI Use Policy

• Approve and maintain the list of approved tools, and assess each new tool for security, privacy, data handling and contract terms.

• Make sure AI work meets data protection law, client confidentiality, copyright and disclosure requirements.

• Keep the agency’s IT and AI setup secure, scalable and suited to a hybrid team.

Skills & Experience
• Proven experience leading digital or AI adoption in a creative, design or professional-services business.

• Hands-on knowledge of current generative AI tools for text, image and workflow automation, and how to apply them to real work.

• Experience integrating software and building automations or internal tools (for example with APIs, low-code platforms or scripting).

• Good working knowledge of data protection, information security and responsible AI practice.

• A confident trainer and communicator who can explain technical ideas in plain language.

• Experience in a design, brand building or marketing is a bonus

• Experience writing AI policies, standards or governance frameworks.

• Experience managing a small team

• A relevant qualification in computing, data, design technology or similar, or equivalent experience.

For careers, enquiries and internships, please email: contact@re-agency.com

