About the role&nbsp;

Our ABM team runs highly targeted programs for the accounts that matter most to RELEX. We want those programs to be even more personalized, more interactive, and faster to launch across channels, without adding manual effort for every new account.&nbsp;

That's where you come in. You'll advise how the ABM team runs and develops five operational areas: paid media, landing page creation, content personalization, targeted direct mail, and analytics. You'll review how each area works today, then design and build the AI-based workflows, templates, and quality guardrails that let the team focus on account strategy, creativity and stakeholder alignment over manual work.&nbsp;

What you'll do&nbsp;

Across all five operational areas&nbsp;

• Map how each area works today, find where time and quality can be improved, and agree a prioritized automation roadmap with the Head of ABM 

• Build and maintain the AI workflows the ABM team uses day to day, with tools such as Claude, n8n, Folloze and HubSpot 

• Partner with Marketing Operations, who own our martech platforms, data, and integrations: build ABM workflows on top of the shared stack, follow its standards, and hand over anything that should become a cross-team capability 

• Agree brand and quality guardrails with Brand &amp; Creative so AI-produced assets can go live with light review 

• Document every workflow and train the team so it runs without you&nbsp;

Ad operations (LinkedIn, Influ2)&nbsp;

• Own the setup and execution model for ABM account and contact level campaigns 

• Build workflows and guardrails that cut the time spent on campaign setup 

• Build workflows that generate on-brand ad variants by account, segment, and buying group role 

• Run channel and tactic experiments to find the right mix of reach, engagement, and conversion activity 

• Close the data feedback loop, so account and contact level engagement flows back to the account team and into ABM planning automatically&nbsp;

Landing page operations&nbsp;

• Build a template and component library the team can use to generate account and segment pages with AI 

• Set standards for personalization depth, and work with ABM designers on a tailored look and feel per account 

• Find opportunities to build deeper, more interactive experiences for prospects&nbsp;

Content build operations&nbsp;

• Build and fine-tune workflows that turn existing RELEX content (research, customer stories, point of view pieces) into account-tailored assets such as one-pagers, guides, and sales follow-up material&nbsp;

Direct mail operations&nbsp;

• Design a direct mail program framework that delivers personalized mailers at scale 

• Own the operating model behind them: vendor setup, address data quality, GDPR compliance, budget, and cost per account 

• Connect every send to a defined sales follow-up, and measure what it contributes&nbsp;

Analytics and reporting&nbsp;

• Define how ABM programs are measured, together with the Head of ABM and Marketing Operations: account reach, engagement, buying group coverage, and pipeline contribution 

• Build and maintain reporting that shows what's working by account, channel, and tactic, so channel and budget decisions rest on evidence rather than assumption 

• Keep campaign data clean and comparable across platforms, including naming conventions, UTM standards, and campaign taxonomy 

• Measure the impact of the AI workflows themselves: time saved, cost per asset, and speed from brief to launch&nbsp;

What we're looking for&nbsp;

• 4+ years in B2B ABM, demand generation, growth marketing, GTM engineering, or marketing operations 

• A working understanding of how B2B paid media runs, ideally on LinkedIn: campaign structure, account and contact list targeting, bidding and budget pacing, and which platform metrics you can and can’t trust 

• A proven track record of designing and shipping AI and automation workflows that other people use, with examples you can walk us through 

• Practical experience working with LLMs: prompt design, structured outputs, connecting models to business data and tools, and evaluating output quality 

• Hands-on experience building automations in n8n, Make, Zapier, Workato, or similar, including APIs, webhooks, JSON, and error handling 

• A process mindset: you can map a workflow, see where it breaks, and design a repeatable replacement 

• Good judgment on quality: you know when AI output is ready to be rolled out and when it isn't&nbsp;

Nice to have&nbsp;

• Enough Python or JavaScript to write, read, and debug automation scripts and API calls 

• Experience with intent and engagement platforms such as 6sense, or contact-level advertising such as Influ2 

• Experience running direct mail or gifting programs in B2B 

• Working knowledge of SQL and at least one BI or reporting tool (for example Power BI, Looker, or Tableau) 

• Background in global enterprise B2B software with long, multi-stakeholder buying cycles&nbsp;

About RELEX&nbsp;

RELEX Solutions creates cutting-edge supply chain and retail planning software. Within our platforms, we have the power and potential to increase adaptability, efficiency, and sustainability in the consumer goods and retail value chain. Our impact is tangible; from sustainability and eliminating waste to delighting customers and delivering great tailored tech solutions, we’re curious and passionate challenge-seekers creating the future of retail today.

We’re currently a global team of 2000+ employees working from offices in the US (Atlanta), UK, Germany, Sweden, Norway, Denmark, France, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Singapore, Australia, and our headquarters in Helsinki, Finland. We work in small teams where everyone’s input is valued. We’re passionate about what we do, we like putting our skills to the test, and we make sure we have fun during the process — because life is supposed to be fun.

RELEX Solutions is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.

About the role&nbsp;

RELEX’s GTM AI team in Sales builds the AI our sellers use every day. We work across three areas. Salesforce holds the record and runs the sales motion. Claude is a primary surface on which our sellers work, utilising our plugins, skills and connectors. Around Salesforce and Claude sit the other applications sellers use, including applications built on RELEX’s own AI platform, Cortex. This role owns Claude and AI applications outside of Salesforce, and will be responsible for building the AI that RELEX's sellers work with every day. You’ll decide how it’s built and build it yourself as part of a team.&nbsp;

What you’ll own&nbsp;

Claude and other AI within the Sales division&nbsp;

• Its plugins, skills and connectors, how they’re organised by role, and how they’re released, supported, and retired.

• What Claude may read and change in Salesforce and related systems, as well as ensuring there are guardrails in place.

• Human-in-the-loop design: What runs autonomously, what requires human involvement, and designing AI use that sharpens seller judgment rather than flattening it. &nbsp;

• Context Portability: What sellers rely on lives in Salesforce and in maintained sources rather than inside an edge system or locally on a machine, so a change of tool doesn’t lead to context loss or significant change effort.

• How Claude and other AI models can be utilised within Sales and Sales Operations, from Claude Managed Agents and engineering workflows, to utilisation of emerging models (e.g. Jev).&nbsp;

Applications&nbsp;

• Sales’ applications outside Salesforce: Ownership and development of Cortex applications within Sales and self-built systems outside of Cortex, as well as consultation on other 3rd party tools’ AI capabilities and how they contribute to the overall strategy and integrated ecosystem.

• How our AI connects to the systems around Salesforce, such as enrichment, intent data, engagement, call recording, content, quotes, and signatures. &nbsp;

• Sales’ voice with the AI Platform team: what Sales needs from the platform, and how Sales data reaches it with adequate security and user permissions.&nbsp;

Quality, safety, and value&nbsp;

• Ensuring RELEX’s AI data-handling policy is applied in your areas: what each AI may see, and under whose permissions.

• How prompts and models are tested before release.&nbsp;

Technical direction outside Salesforce&nbsp;

• Greenfield scope to build innovative AI applications for our Sales division, and the authority to lead its architecture and development.

• A visible seat at the table, providing technical leadership in your area.

• Keeping up to date with both Anthropic’s and the platform team’s roadmaps, proposing new capability when it serves a goal, and proposing retirements for what it replaces.&nbsp;

What you’ll bring&nbsp;

• At least five years of building software, with significant experience building AI applications or agents running in production.&nbsp;

• Strong knowledge of TypeScript or Python. Experience with APIs, OAuth and identity, and webhooks, as well as Model Context Protocol.

• Experience integrating with a system of record, such as Salesforce, through its APIs and permission model.

• Hands-on experience with cloud hosting, covering deployment, secrets, and monitoring.

• Experience with data protection, e.g. permissions, data residency, and what an AI should and shouldn’t see.

• An understanding of how sellers work, and the instinct to keep people’s judgment where it adds value.

• Clear writing, e.g. for decision requests, definitions of done and documentation.

• A record of getting things done through teams you don’t manage, such as platform teams, IT, operations and sales leaders.&nbsp;

What we’d consider an advantage&nbsp;

• Experience with Claude plugins/skills/hooks, Claude Code, and Anthropic’s API or Agent SDK.

• Enough Salesforce development (APIs, connected apps, Flows) to work at the seams with our Salesforce engineer.

• Experience with Sales tools across areas such as sales engagement, lead enrichment, intent, call recording, CPQ, etc.

• A background in retail, manufacturing, or supply chain.&nbsp;

About RELEX

RELEX Solutions creates cutting-edge supply chain and retail planning software. Within our platforms, we have the power and potential to increase adaptability, efficiency, and sustainability in the consumer goods and retail value chain. Our impact is tangible; from sustainability and eliminating waste to delighting customers and delivering great tailored tech solutions, we’re curious and passionate challenge-seekers creating the future of retail today.

We’re currently a global team of 2000+ employees working from offices in the US (Atlanta), UK, Germany, Sweden, Norway, Denmark, France, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Singapore, Australia, and our headquarters in Helsinki, Finland. We work in small teams where everyone’s input is valued. We’re passionate about what we do, we like putting our skills to the test, and we make sure we have fun during the process — because life is supposed to be fun.

RELEX Solutions is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.

