• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field.

• Proficiency in Python programming is essential.

• Strong understanding of cloud technologies, including AWS services such as S3, Lambda, and DynamoDB.

• Demonstrated experience with database management and backend development.

• Familiarity with tools like EMR and Spark for data processing.

• Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team.

• Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills.

• Prior experience in financial or mortgage industries is a plus, but not required.

• This is a remote position and requires the ability to work in a home office environment with the ability to work effectively surrounded by moderate home environment noise.

How to Apply

Interested in joining our team?

Please send your resume and cover letter to info@sannik.co.uk, indicating the position you're applying for in the subject line. We look forward to hearing from you!

Senior Quality Analyst

3 The Quadrant, Richmond, UK

Job Type

Full Time

Workspace

Hybrid - Remote

Salary (GBP)

​

About the Role

• Lead investigation and development of new tools and methodologies to support the quality assurance initiatives and proactively identify areas for improvement related to quality assurance tools and methodologies
• Demonstrate knowledge of Garmin product specifications, capabilities and operation related to the market segment being supported
• Motivate and drive accountability to project teams and stakeholders in pursuit of successfully delivering quality goals
• Design test plans, scenarios, scripts and/or procedures of significant complexity, in accordance with established Garmin test procedures - including analysis, review and tracing of requirements as necessary
• Serve as the voice of the customer in product design reviews to provide input on functional requirements, product designs, schedules, resource needs, target release dates and/or potential problems
• Demonstrate ability to conduct usability tests and communicate results to product owners
• Document defects in defect management system and report defects to developers
• Collect and analyze test results and beta user feedback (when applicable), and recommend enhancements to, or provide gap analysis of, test methods used in order to enhance efficiency and test coverage
• Deliver project status and summary information as needed to all levels of leadership
• Investigate and verify issues reported to quality assurance for validity and reproducibility and provide leadership in defect analysis to create new test cases and methods to improve test coverage
• Recommend new testing approaches to accommodate schedules and resource constraints
• Verify software modifications in new software versions to prepare for implementation
• Assist in test case maintenance as necessary to keep repository current

Requirements

What we are looking for?

We are seeking a full-time Senior Quality Analyst. In this role, you will be responsible for providing leadership of quality assurance activities for complex features within Garmin consumer products and/or software in a team-oriented environment.

