• Bachelor's Degree AND a minimum of 5 years relevant experience OR a minimum of 9 years equivalent combination of education and experience

• Bachelor’s Degree OR a minimum of 4 years equivalent combination of education and experience

• Relevant experience or training in product and/or software quality assurance processes and methodologies related to a Garmin core product market and in creating test plans and conducting usability tests for large projects.

How to Apply

Interested in joining our team?

Please send your resume and cover letter to info@sannik.co.uk, indicating the position you're applying for in the subject line. We look forward to hearing from you!

Senior Web Developer

3 The Quadrant, Coventry, UK

Job Type

Full Time

Workspace

Hybrid - Remote

Salary (GBP)

41500

About the Role

The development team is an application group. They enhance and maintain websites and applications for both internal and external customers. The team provides programming support for all web projects and internal applications and will be an integral part in modernizing the current application.

This position will be a full-stack developer involved in design and architecture of the web system.

