 Benefits

 We offer a competitive salary and benefits package and will provide you with opportunities to grow, flourish, and achieve great things. Our benefits include:

 Pension

Careers

As a dynamic and growing company, Software Tec Lab offers staff a challenging and rewarding career opportunity. The engineering ethos is embedded in the culture of the organisation and the ability to work at the cutting edge of technology will be enough for many to consider us a natural choice to advance their career. 

We are building a world-class company, and are always on the lookout for talent that wants to make a difference. If you have a significant contribution you can make, then give us a call. No matter whether you are a graduate or an experienced engineer, if you are interested in joining a dynamic and growing company, send your c.v. and a covering letter to career@SoftwareTecLab.co.uk

Software, Embedded and Cloud platform Developers – we really want to hear from you !

Current Opportunities

Software Development Consultant (C/C++, C#, Python) [Glasgow]

Software Tec Lab – Glasgow G2 2UW

Job Description

Software Tec Lab is a specialist software development consultancy based in Glasgow. We deliver tailored software engineering for clients developing pioneering electronic devices, apps, and cloud solutions.

We are seeking a self-motivated, software consultant with multiplatform experience to help develop innovative technology solutions for our clients. This is a high-profile, hands-on consultancy role, with opportunity for you to benefit from lots of variety, and be rewarded for successful development projects.

Essential Technical skills:

• 3+ years experience of hands-on coding for commercial software;

• Proficient in writing clean, well-documented code in C/C++, C#, and Python;

• Experienced in implementing .NET/C# backend and APIs;

• Skilled with C/C++ applications & drivers;

• Comfortable with integration of IoT devices / embedded systems;

• Develops high-quality code, employing unit testing and adhering to best coding practices;

• Full lifecycle software development background.

The following desirable skills are a plus for the candidate (where more is better)

• Degree qualification in Software, Computing/IT, Electronics or equivalent;

• Broad software development skills are preferred (C++, C#, Python, Java, JavaScript…);

• Development experience for multiple platforms (e.g. Linux, Windows, Real-time embedded);

• Familiarity with AWS/Azure Cloud systems and databases is an advantage;

• Proficiency using GIT;

• Someone who leads and is committed to ensuring quality is built in.

We are building a highly-capable software development team, who will share in the rewards of our client success. The role is office based and arrangements for periods of home-working can be explored.

Additional Information:

• No agencies please.

• Any offer of employment will be subject to the successful candidate holding the right to work in the UK.

Job Type: Full-time, Part-time, Contract

Spaulding Ridge is an advisory and IT implementation firm. We help global organizations get financial clarity into the complex, daily sales, and operational decisions that impact profitable revenue generations, efficient operational performance, and reliable financial management.

At Spaulding Ridge, we believe all business is personal. Core to our values is our relationships with our clients, our business partners, our team, and the global community. Our employees dedicate their time to helping our clients transform their business, from strategy through implementation and business transformation.&nbsp;

What You Will Do and Learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

We are seeking an Engagement Lead to join our Revenue Excellence practice in Europe. In this role, you will oversee relationships with enterprise clients while leading the successful delivery of Salesforce, CLM, and adjacent business transformation engagements.&nbsp;&nbsp;

This role is responsible for leading delivery across complex client engagements, strengthening long-term enterprise relationships, and identifying opportunities for growth across functions, business units, and regions.&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities:&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Build and maintain strong, trust-based relationships with a portfolio of major enterprise clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Develop a deep understanding of client business processes, priorities, and requirements to deliver tailored, meaningful solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Expand relationships with existing clients by proactively identifying and proposing value add opportunities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Advise clients on Salesforce, CLM, and related technology solutions&nbsp;

• Lead multi-disciplinary internal teams, effectively deploying resources while supporting team members’ development and progression.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Ensure timely delivery of products, services, and project milestones in alignment with client expectations and engagement goals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Act as the primary communication bridge between clients and internal teams, ensuring alignment, clarity, and transparency.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Address client issues quickly and strategically, managing escalations and maintaining strong client trust.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Partner with Sales and Account teams to identify and drive new engagement opportunities that support long-term client growth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Prepare and deliver regular status updates, performance insights, and forecasts using key account metrics for both internal and external stakeholders.&nbsp;

What You Bring:&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Proven experience as an engagement lead, project manager, or client relationship manager within technology or professional services.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Strong background in solution delivery, with experience shaping client outcomes based on business needs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Experience delivering solutions centered around Salesforce, CLM platforms, or related cloud-based applications.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Exceptional communication, stakeholder management, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to influence across all organizational levels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Strong problem-solving abilities and confidence navigating negotiations and challenging client scenarios.&nbsp;

Spaulding Ridge’s Commitment to an Inclusive Workplace&nbsp;

When we engage the expertise, insights, and creativity of people from all walks of life, we become a better organization, we deliver superior services to clients, and we transform our communities and world for the better.

At Spaulding Ridge, we believe our team should reflect the rich diversity of society and we take seriously the responsibility to cultivate a workplace where every bandmate feels accepted, respected, and valued for who they are. We do this by creating a culture of trust and belonging, through practices and policies that support inclusion, and through our employee led Employee Resource Groups (ERGs): CRE (Cultural Race and Ethnicity), Women Elevate, PROUD and Mental Wellness Alliance.

The company is committed to offering Equal Employment Opportunity and to providing reasonable accommodation to applicants with physical and/or mental disabilities. If you are interested in applying for employment with Spaulding Ridge and are in need of accommodation or special assistance to navigate our website or to complete your application, please send an e-mail with your request to our VP of Human Resources, Cara Halladay (challaday@spauldingridge.com). Requests for reasonable accommodation will be considered on a case-by-case basis.

Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their age, race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status or disability.

