 Full Time / Permanent
 Location
 Bristol
 Job Summary
 Who you are 

We are looking for an enthusiastic and motivated Real Estate Solicitor/Associate (ideally NQ-4 years' PQE) to join our highly regarded Bristol-based team on a permanent, full-time basis.

Ranked Band 1 in Legal 500 South West 2026, our Real Estate team advises a diverse client base including institutional investors, developers, lenders, local authorities and private clients. We work across key sectors including Investment, Real Estate Finance, Housebuilding and Development, Energy and Infrastructure, and Commercial Development.

Working closely with the Partners and an experienced team of real estate specialists, you'll play a key role in advising on a broad range of landlord and tenant matters, with a particular focus on retail leasing and property acquisitions for pension schemes.

Our client base includes a fantastic mix of national and household-name businesses, including Subway, Taco Bell and Curtis Banks. You'll have the opportunity to work on high-quality matters, develop strong client relationships and take on significant responsibility from an early stage in your career. With direct access to experienced partners and senior lawyers, you'll benefit from excellent mentoring and support, alongside genuine opportunities for progression as part of a successful and expanding practice.

You'll also be encouraged to get involved in business development activities, helping to strengthen existing client relationships, develop new opportunities and support the continued growth of Ashfords' Real Estate practice.

What you'll do 

As an excellent communicator with strong technical and organisational skills, you’ll be comfortable managing competing priorities and working to deadlines. Ideally, you'll have a solid grounding in real estate work, with experience gained at a national, regional or City firm, and exposure to either retail property or SIPP/SSAS transactions.

With a keen eye for detail and a commercial approach, you'll be confident advising a range of clients and delivering an exceptional client experience. Building strong, long-term relationships is central to our success, so you'll be able to demonstrate a genuine commitment to understanding clients' objectives and supporting their wider business needs.

We're looking for someone who is ambitious, self-motivated and keen to continue developing their technical expertise and market knowledge. You'll have a genuine interest in the real estate sector, keeping up to date with market trends and developments to help provide practical, commercially focused advice to clients.

In return, we'll support you in building your professional profile, expanding your network and developing your business development skills through access to industry events, conferences and client-facing opportunities.

Your Career. Our Commitment.

At Ashfords, we believe in more than just doing great work - we believe in building a great place to work.

When you join us, you become part of a team where everything we do is underpinned by our four core values: Be Open, Think Team, Make a Difference and Always Grow. These values shape who we are and how we work - they guide our decisions, influence our culture, and drive the way we support our people, clients and communities.

With a clear focus on innovation, community involvement, and supporting a healthy work-life balance, we are committed to building an environment where our people can have a rewarding and meaningful career.

Whilst we recognise that every career journey is unique, we will be ambitious for you, giving you the tools, trust, and opportunities to develop your career, your way.

Our goal? To help you realise your full potential as part of a forward-thinking team. 

Our offer

We know that our people are at the heart of everything we do – and that’s why we’re committed to supporting your wellbeing, growth and work-life balance.

Beyond our benefits package, you’ll be encouraged, no matter what your role or career level, to get involved in our Responsible Business programme, where you’ll support initiatives such as charity fundraising, environmental causes and our employee led diversity and inclusion groups.

You can find out more about our benefits by visiting the Reward & Wellbeing page on our website.

What’s next?

Our recruitment process typically involves two stages, which are designed not only to explore your skills and experience but also to give you a real insight into what it’s like to work at Ashfords. Throughout the process, our dedicated Talent Attraction team will be here to support you every step of the way.

We believe that building a firm with a wide range of perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences drives innovation and strengthens our teams, and we welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds.

To support your growth, we offer ongoing training and development opportunities to help you reach your full potential – so even if you don’t feel you match all the requirements of the job role, we’d still love to hear from you.

At Ashfords, we’re committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace where everyone feels respected, valued, and empowered to succeed.

If you require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or would like to discuss anything regarding your application, please contact us at talentattraction@ashfords.co.uk.

For an informal and confidential discussion about this opportunity, please contact Toby Tompkins, Talent Attraction Manager - t.tompkins@ashfords.co.uk.

Or apply now, and we will be in touch with you as soon as possible.

Specialized in civil engineering and engineering structures, Bouygues Travaux Publics is one of the world leaders in the fields of land use planning and sustainable infrastructure construction. Bouygues Travaux Publics is committed to diversity and is open to all talents.

Sizewell C is one of the UK’s most significant infrastructure and energy projects. The programme will deliver a new 3.2-gigawatt nuclear power station in Suffolk, providing reliable low-carbon electricity for approximately six million homes and supporting the UK’s long-term energy security.

We are looking for an experienced Programme Integrator / Planner to join the Civil Works Alliance (CWA), supporting the delivery of the CWA-wide Construction Services programme at Sizewell C.

This role will be central to ensuring effective integration and coordination across preconstruction, Advanced Work Packaging (AWP), readiness, engineering, construction delivery, commercial and logistics teams.

Working across multiple disciplines and project interfaces, you will help ensure that activities are properly planned, sequenced and coordinated, with scope, dependencies, constraints and readiness requirements clearly understood before work is released for execution.

This is an opportunity to contribute to the successful delivery of a major national infrastructure programme, helping establish the coordination, planning and governance processes required to support safe, predictable and efficient construction.

## The Role

As Programme Integrator / Planner, you will act as a central coordination point across Construction Services, ensuring that programme-wide activities, interfaces and dependencies are effectively integrated from preconstruction through to construction delivery.

You will work closely with planning, engineering, construction, AWP, readiness, commercial and logistics teams to develop and maintain integrated plans, coordinate Construction Work Packages (CWPs) and support the transition of planned activities into execution.

A key part of the role will be identifying and managing constraints, assumptions, interfaces and dependencies that could affect programme performance, ensuring that potential issues are visible, assigned and resolved in a timely manner.

You will also coordinate readiness requirements, monitor progress against key milestones and provide clear, traceable reporting to support project governance and informed decision-making.

The role will require a proactive approach to stakeholder engagement, information management and continuous improvement, ensuring that planning and integration processes remain aligned with the evolving needs of the project and support effective delivery across the CWA.

## Key Responsibilities

- Coordinate and integrate programme-wide activities across Construction Services, ensuring alignment between preconstruction, engineering, AWP, readiness, construction delivery, commercial and logistics functions;
- Develop, maintain and monitor integrated programme plans, ensuring that activities, milestones, dependencies and interfaces are clearly identified and coordinated;
- Support the development, coordination and implementation of Construction Work Packages (CWPs), ensuring that scope, sequencing, interfaces, deliverables and responsibilities are clearly defined;
- Work closely with AWP teams to align engineering deliverables, procurement, materials availability, construction planning and work package development;
- Identify, track and manage programme constraints, assumptions, risks, opportunities and interdependencies, coordinating appropriate mitigation and resolution actions;
- Coordinate construction readiness activities, ensuring that required information, resources, materials, access, permits and other prerequisites are appropriately considered within plans and work packages;
- Support readiness assessments, launch reviews and mobilisation reviews to verify that activities are sufficiently prepared for safe and effective execution;
- Monitor progress against programme milestones, identify emerging delays or conflicts, and work with relevant stakeholders to develop recovery actions and maintain delivery priorities;
- Facilitate coordination meetings and integration reviews, ensuring that key interfaces, decisions, actions and outstanding constraints are clearly documented and followed through to resolution;
- Produce and maintain programme integration reports, readiness dashboards, constraint registers and associated management information to support governance and project decision-making;
- Ensure that programme information, assumptions, dependencies and decisions are recorded accurately, consistently and in a traceable manner;
- Support effective communication between engineering, planning, construction, procurement, commercial, logistics and supply chain teams;
- Identify opportunities to improve planning, work packaging, readiness coordination and programme integration processes;
- Capture lessons learned and promote the consistent application of best practices across Construction Services; and
- Support the effective transition from preconstruction and planning into construction execution, ensuring continuity of information, alignment of priorities and visibility of outstanding actions.

## Essential Skills & Experience

We are looking for candidates who can demonstrate:

- Proven experience in programme integration, project planning, coordination or project controls within construction, civil engineering or major infrastructure projects;
- Experience coordinating multidisciplinary teams and integrating activities across engineering, planning, procurement, logistics and construction functions;
- A sound understanding of construction planning, sequencing, dependencies and the coordination of activities from preconstruction through to delivery;
- Experience identifying and managing programme constraints, risks, assumptions, interfaces and dependencies;
- Familiarity with Advanced Work Packaging (AWP), Construction Work Packages (CWPs) and the coordination of construction readiness requirements;
- Experience developing, maintaining and monitoring integrated plans, progress reports, dashboards and management information;
- The ability to analyse programme information, identify potential delivery issues and support the development of practical mitigation and recovery measures;
- Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, coordinate stakeholders and maintain accurate records of actions and decisions;
- Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to facilitate alignment across multidisciplinary teams and organisational interfaces;
- Experience supporting project governance, coordination meetings, readiness reviews and structured reporting processes;
- A proactive and structured approach to problem-solving, with a strong focus on programme performance and delivery readiness;
- A degree-level qualification in construction management, engineering, project management or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant professional experience; and
- The ability to work effectively within a complex, fast-paced and collaborative project environment.

## Desirable Experience

Experience in one or more of the following would be particularly advantageous:

- Nuclear, energy or other highly regulated infrastructure projects;
- Major civil engineering, construction or large-scale infrastructure programmes;
- Advanced Work Packaging (AWP) methodologies and the development and management of Construction Work Packages;
- Construction readiness planning, work release processes and mobilisation reviews;
- Integrated programme planning, project controls and management reporting;
- Planning and coordination of interfaces between design, engineering, procurement, logistics and construction;
- Constraint management, risk and opportunity management, and structured action tracking;
- Project governance and reporting within an alliance, joint venture or collaborative contracting environment;
- Planning and reporting tools, dashboards and data visualisation platforms used to monitor programme performance;
- Professional membership of a recognised institution, such as APM, CIOB or ICE; and
- A recognised project management qualification, such as APM PMQ or PRINCE2.

## Personal Attributes

We are looking for someone who is:

- **Highly organised** – able to coordinate multiple activities, manage competing priorities and maintain clear oversight of programme deliverables;
- **Analytical and detail-oriented** – capable of identifying dependencies, constraints, inconsistencies and potential impacts on delivery;
- **Collaborative** – comfortable working across engineering, construction, planning, commercial, logistics and supply chain teams;
- **Proactive and solutions-focused** – able to anticipate issues, drive actions and support timely resolution of programme constraints;
- **Programme-focused** – understands the importance of sequencing, milestones, readiness and dependencies in achieving predictable delivery;
- **An effective communicator** – able to facilitate discussions, align stakeholders and present programme information clearly;
- **Accountable and structured** – ensures that actions, assumptions, decisions and interfaces are properly recorded and followed through;
- **Adaptable** – able to respond to changing priorities and evolving requirements within a complex project environment; and
- **Committed to continuous improvement** – keen to identify opportunities to improve planning processes, coordination practices and delivery performance.

## Project Environment

The role forms part of the Sizewell C Civil Works Alliance (CWA), bringing together Sizewell C, Balfour Beatty, Bouygues Travaux Publics and Laing O’Rourke to support the delivery of one of the UK’s largest infrastructure programmes.

You will work across the CWA-wide Construction Services function, interacting with preconstruction, engineering, planning, AWP, readiness, construction delivery, commercial and logistics teams.

The role will focus on ensuring that programme activities are effectively integrated, that construction work packages are developed and coordinated in line with delivery requirements, and that constraints and readiness requirements are addressed before work moves into execution.

Operating across multiple teams and organisational interfaces, you will help establish clear plans, reliable reporting and effective coordination mechanisms to support safe and efficient construction delivery.

This is an opportunity to take on a key programme integration role within a major nuclear infrastructure project, contributing to improved programme visibility, stronger delivery readiness and the successful coordination of complex civil engineering activities.

## What We Offer

As part of the CWA, you will have the opportunity to contribute to a nationally significant infrastructure programme supported by Sizewell C and its three delivery partners: Balfour Beatty, Bouygues Travaux Publics and Laing O’Rourke.

You will work within a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment, gaining exposure to complex programme integration, construction planning and delivery coordination on one of the UK’s most strategically important energy projects.

The role offers the opportunity to work alongside experienced industry professionals and contribute directly to the planning, coordination and delivery processes that underpin a major infrastructure programme.

The employment package includes a competitive salary, annual leave, pension and flexible benefits, in accordance with the applicable employing organisation’s arrangements.

